problems.problem:
Four married couples meet for a game of chess. They draw lots to form four groups of two players. Knowing that
Beatrice plays against Eddy;
Alice plays against Clara's husband;
Freddy plays against Guy's wife;
Doris plays against Alice's husband;
Guy plays against Eddy's wife,
can one tell who Hubert's wife is? Justify your answer.

Determine all functions $f, g\colon \mathbb{R} \to \mathbb{R}$ satisfying the following conditions:
(i) $2f(s) - g(s) = f(t) - t$ for all real $s$ and $t$;
(ii) $f(s)g(s) \ge s + 1$ for all real $s$.
